libsmb2 6.2: never sign or seal a guest or null session (no session key).

When session setup returns SMB2_SESSION_FLAG_IS_GUEST or IS_NULL, the client
gets no session key (MS-SMB2 3.2.5.3.1). libsmb2 6.2 still derives keys and
turns on sealing, either from IS_ENCRYPT_DATA or from the share's
SMB2_SHAREFLAG_ENCRYPT_DATA. A server with "smb encrypt = desired" then drops
the connection. With this patch a guest or null session:
  * never signs or seals, and skips key derivation;
  * ignores the share's encrypt flag (a server that requires encryption
    refuses the tree connect itself);
  * does not sign its SMB 3.1.1 TREE_CONNECT (lib/pdu.c), which 3.1.1
    otherwise signs even without session signing;
  * fails with -EACCES when the caller asked for signing.

Origin: Mediahro lane B2 (NET-001), mediahro PR #21 at a494b58 (5 hunks;
first carried from PR #20 at b5951f8),
packages/mediahro_ffi/test/network/patches/libsmb2-6.2-guest-session.patch.

Licence: this is a modification of libsmb2, which is LGPL-2.1-or-later, and
the change is under the same licence. The modified source is offered with
the release's mediahro-deps-sources.tar, which carries this patch next to the
